{{~##
   What every generated Swift file starts with: the banner and the one import.

   Shared because the output is a file per table, and a header repeated in four templates is
   four places for one of them to lose the `DO NOT EDIT` line - which is what the sweep
   recognises its own output by.

   No import of the reader. Swift has no import of names within a module, and the reader is
   compiled as part of the same target - which also means this target has none of the
   per-file symbol list the Kotlin one has to keep current.

   Foundation in every file, including the ones that do not reach it: an unused import is
   not a warning in Swift, and the alternative is working out per file whether a template
   will render a path or a dictionary - a calculation with nothing to check it.
##~}}
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Generated by Tabbit. DO NOT EDIT.
//
// Changes to this file may cause incorrect behavior and will be lost if the code is
// regenerated.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

import Foundation
